  "notes": "Almost all of this PR is a new optional JAX backend: the new files jax_backend.py and utils/jax_geometry.py, plus the backend=\"jax\" branches in chain.py. You can only reach that code through a `backend` keyword argument, which base does not accept. The only changes to the existing numpy path are trivial: the length check in forward_kinematics moves earlier, and a `backend` keyword argument is passed through. I wrote a workload that runs numpy IK and FK on the poppy_torso arm. Every check passed except head coverage: base coverage was 0.9, outputs were equal, base ran in about 3 s and the no-network run passed. Head coverage was 0.115 without jax and 0.238 with jax installed in both venvs, both below the 0.5 threshold. I removed jax again, so both venvs are back to their original state."
